<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Champions</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 546 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a> · Also known as Battle of the 300 Champions</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Champions was fought about 546 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> for the border district of Thyreatis. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, each side chose 300 men to settle the dispute; two Argives and one Spartan, Othryades, survived, and both sides claimed victory. A full battle followed in which Sparta won, gaining the Thyreatis and confirming its supremacy in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>.</p></div>
